.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH murk-mcp 1  "mcp " 
.SH NAME
murk\-mcp \- Run an MCP (Model Context Protocol) stdio server for AI agents (experimental)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmurk mcp\fR [\fB\-\-vault\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-exec\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run an MCP (Model Context Protocol) stdio server for AI agents (experimental)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-vault\fR \fI<VAULT>\fR [default: .murk]
Vault filename
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-exec\fR
Enable the murk_exec tool, which runs commands with the grant\*(Aqs secrets injected

Off by default. The tool runs arbitrary commands as this user. The injected secrets are limited to the grant, but the command itself is not sandboxed.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
